layout: lr
title: "OTC interest-rate swap lifecycle"
subtitle: "Execution through novation — with regulatory reporting and CCP clearing branches"
caption: "Source: examples/37-otc-swap-lifecycle.melk"
legend: on

# An OTC IRS (interest-rate swap) lifecycle modelled after the FpML
# process view. Trade flows left to right along the data spine:
#
#   execution  -> two counterparties agree economics (rate, tenor,
#                 notional, schedule).
#   confirm    -> bilateral confirmation matched on a platform
#                 (MarkitWire, MarkitServ, etc.).
#   clearing   -> trade submitted to a CCP (LCH SwapClear, CME, EUREX)
#                 for novation.
#   settlement -> periodic coupon exchange + margin movement until
#                 maturity.
#
# Two branches model the regulated side-effects:
#
#   - `report` (down branch) — trade is reported to a trade repository
#     (DTCC GTR, REGIS-TR) per Dodd-Frank / EMIR / MiFIR. This fires
#     regardless of whether the trade clears.
#   - `bilateral` (up branch) — uncleared trades that fail the
#     clearing threshold or asset-class mandate stay bilateral and
#     post initial margin under UMR. Tagged `future` because UMR
#     phase-in scope still expands; tagged `critical` because UMR
#     non-compliance carries regulatory penalties.

execution  { shape: rect,      label: "execution\n(voice / SEF)" }
confirm    { shape: rect,      label: "confirmation\n(MarkitWire)" }
clearing   { shape: diamond,   label: "clearing\neligibility?" }
ccp        { shape: rect,      label: "CCP novation\n(LCH SwapClear)" }
settlement { shape: cylinder,  label: "settlement\n+ margin" }
maturity   { shape: roundrect, label: "maturity\n/ termination" }

report     { shape: roundrect, label: "trade repository\n(DTCC GTR)" }
bilateral  { shape: roundrect, label: "bilateral\n+ UMR margin", tags: [critical] }

pipeline trade_flow: execution -> confirm -> clearing -> ccp -> settlement -> maturity

# Regulatory reporting fires off the confirmation step — every trade,
# cleared or not, gets reported within the T+1 window.
branch reg-report:right: confirm -> report

# Uncleared path — trade fails the clearing-eligibility check and
# stays bilateral. Up-branch so cleared (down) and bilateral (up)
# read as the two possible outcomes of the diamond.
branch uncleared:left: clearing -> bilateral
